The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
for (i = 0; i < npages; i += (1 << max_order)) {
    ...
}
```
Reason:
The loop in `kvm_gmem_populate()` iterates over a potentially large number of pages without checking for pending signals. This can cause the function to run indefinitely if a signal is received, leading to unresponsiveness in the system.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (signal_pending(current)) {
    ret = -EINTR;
    break;
}
```
Reason:
This addition checks for pending signals during each iteration of the loop. If a signal is detected, it sets the return value to `-EINTR` and breaks out of the loop, allowing the function to respond to interrupts and preventing indefinite execution.

